  "findings": [
    {
      "symbols": [
        "sensorarrayUsbSinkPublishClass",
        "sensorarraySerialQueueRecord"
      ],
      "evidence": "Read and unread cases use the same already-encoded complete packet. Owner path has no repeated scientific formatter. QueueRecord copies only after a CPU-only normal slot is claimed; saturated unread queues reject before that copy. Normal payload pool prefers PSRAM with explicit internal fallback, so source intent alone is not proof of its runtime address."
    },
    {
      "symbols": [
        "sensorarraySerialOtgTxTask",
        "sensorarrayUsbOtgOwnerWrite"
      ],
      "evidence": "One USB task owns the formal stream. It advances accepted offset exactly by returned byte count, preserves a partial formal record across turns and prevents CTRL interleaving into its prefix. Errors and TTL expire with counted drop/delimiter. No same accepted prefix retransmission was found."
    },
    {
      "symbols": [
        "sensorarrayUsbOtgOwnerPoll",
        "sensorarraySerialTxCheckpoint"
      ],
      "evidence": "OwnerPoll consumes at most16TinyUSB events per iteration and bounded RX bytes; no-progress notification waits one tick. Progress drains remain guarded by shared WorkBudget. This is bounded active service, not proof that USB service has no impact on other Core0tasks."
    },
    {
      "symbols": [
        "sensorarrayUsbOtgOwnerWrite",
        "tu_edpt_stream_write",
        "tu_edpt_stream_write_xfer"
      ],
      "evidence": "Normal reader allows sustained CPU pool->TinyUSB FIFO->internal DMA EP-buffer copying and completion-event service. Full-speed MPS remains64; EP-buffer512 batches eight packets. DMA does not remove FIFO/copy/ownerCPU work. In unread hold, class FIFO eventually stops accepting and app queue drops reduce this work."
    },
    {
      "symbols": [
        "sensorarraySerialOtgTxTask",
        "sensorarrayUsbOtgOwnerCanWrite",
        "sensorarrayUsbOtgOwnerWrite"
      ],
      "evidence": "Minor existing redundancy: caller checks CanWrite and OwnerWrite immediately checks it again. TinyUSB stream_write auto-flushes when FIFO count>=MPS; OwnerWrite unconditionally calls explicit flush, which usually just finds endpointbusy after a600B write. Source confirms redundant checks, but no target cost measurement establishes a useful performance gain."
    },
